 2012 at Henson, Conway and Capitol Studios in California, Electric Lady Studios in New York City, and Gang Recording Studio in Paris, France.\nFollowing the minimal production of their previous album, Human After All, Daft Punk recruited session musicians with the help of Chris Caswell to perform live instrumentation and limited the use of electronic instruments to drum machines, a custom-built modular synthesizer and vintage vocoders. It combines disco, progressive rock and pop, with contributions by Paul Jackson Jr., Giorgio Moroder, Chilly Gonzales, Julian Casablancas, Paul Williams, Caswell, Pharrell Williams, Nile Rodgers, Todd Edwards, Panda Bear and DJ Falcon.\n\nFrom Wikipedia ("},{"navigationEndpoint":{"urlEndpoint":{"target":"TARGET_NEW_WINDOW","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_Access_Memories"}},"text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_..."},{"text":") under Creative Commons Attribution CC-BY-SA 3.0 ("},{"navigationEndpoint":{"urlEndpoint":{"target":"TARGET_NEW_WINDOW","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/legalcode"}},"text":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/..."},{"text":")"}]},"shelfStyle":"MUSIC_SHELF_STYLE_OPEN_DIALOG_ON_CLICK"}},"secondSubtitle":{"runs":[{"text":"13 songs"},{"text":" • "},{"text":"1 hour, 14 minutes"}]},"straplineTextOne":{"runs":[{"navigationEndpoint":{"browseEndpoint":{"browseEndpointContextSupportedConfigs":{"browseEndpointContextMusicConfig":{"pageType":"MUSIC_PAGE_TYPE_ARTIST"}},"browseId":"UCRr1xG_2WIDs18a6cIiCxeA"}},"text":"Daft Punk"}]},"straplineThumbnail":{"musicThumbnailRenderer":{"thumbnail":{"thumbnails":[{"height":60,"url":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/qLhu6Py_4_xoBsoubKQsXlhOQGqU9YU1ZRAbFusF0LlrPkXbbpu7bEh-k_ZtE4JwLgubvucAQqcK1hRk=w60-h60-p-l90-rj","width":60},{"height":120,"url":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/qLhu6Py_4_xoBsoubKQsXlhOQGqU9YU1ZRAbFusF0LlrPkXbbpu7bEh-k_ZtE4JwLgubvucAQqcK1hRk=w120-h120-p-l90-rj","width":120},{"height":226,"url":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.co